\newlabel{fig:case_study_alert}{{3a}{8}{\textbf {Alert} (Jan 2026): Querying snack spending over past 6 months reveals 63 transactions (\textyen 30,088) with peaks near \textyen 1,000, prompting a decision to cut back}{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:case_study_alert}{{a}{8}{\textbf {Alert} (Jan 2026): Querying snack spending over past 6 months reveals 63 transactions (\textyen 30,088) with peaks near \textyen 1,000, prompting a decision to cut back}{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig:case_study_confirm}{{3b}{8}{\textbf {Confirmation} (June 2026): Period comparison confirms an 84.7\% reduction in snack spending (\textyen 38,453 $\to $ \textyen 5,893). Higher average transaction (\textyen 506 $\to $ \textyen 655) confirms fewer purchases were the main reason for reduction in spending}{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:case_study_confirm}{{b}{8}{\textbf {Confirmation} (June 2026): Period comparison confirms an 84.7\% reduction in snack spending (\textyen 38,453 $\to $ \textyen 5,893). Higher average transaction (\textyen 506 $\to $ \textyen 655) confirms fewer purchases were the main reason for reduction in spending}{figure.caption.16}{}}
